## 2. Request Classification

Determine the request type before generating any output:

| Request Type                 | Action                                                    |
| ---------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------- |
| New Application              | Generate Chapter 1, 2, and 3 (all)                        |
| New Use Case – Major Change | Update Chapter 2 and Chapter 3                            |
| New Use Case – Minor Change | Update Chapter 3 only                                     |
| EFDNA – Minor Change        | Update 3.0 Integration Layer + new 3.40.x Consumption doc |
| EFDNA – Major Change        | Update Chapter 2 + 3.0 + new 3.40.x Consumption doc       |

### Major Change Triggers

- Introducing a new upstream/downstream system
- Changing system or integration architecture
- Introducing a new integration flow or protocol
- Modifying data flow or payload structure between systems
- New security boundary or network zone crossing

### Minor Change Triggers

- Adding or modifying a database table/field
- Updating internal transformation logic
- Adding configuration parameters
- Small implementation updates with no architectural impact

