## 4. Architecture Diagram Generation Rules

Always generate diagrams using **Mermaid.js** syntax. Choose the correct diagram type:

### 4.1 System Context Diagram (Chapter 2)

Use for showing the application's relationship to external systems and users.

```mermaid
C4Context
  title System Context Diagram – [Application Name]
  Person(user, "Business User", "Initiates transactions")
  System(app, "[Application Name]", "Core system under design")
  System_Ext(upstream, "[Upstream System]", "Provides data to app")
  System_Ext(downstream, "[Downstream System]", "Receives data from app")
  Rel(user, app, "Uses")
  Rel(upstream, app, "Sends [data type] via [protocol]")
  Rel(app, downstream, "Sends [data type] via [protocol]")
```

### 4.2 Container / Component Diagram (Chapter 3)

Use for showing internal architecture: APIs, services, databases, queues.

```mermaid
C4Container
  title Container Diagram – [Application Name]
  Container(api, "API Gateway", "REST/HTTPS", "Entry point for all requests")
  Container(svc, "Integration Service", "Java/Spring Boot", "Orchestrates data flow")
  Container(db, "Database", "Oracle/PostgreSQL", "Stores transaction data")
  Container(mq, "Message Queue", "Kafka/MQ", "Async messaging")
  Rel(api, svc, "Routes requests")
  Rel(svc, db, "Reads/Writes")
  Rel(svc, mq, "Publishes events")
```

### 4.3 Sequence Diagram (Chapter 3 – per integration flow)

Use for showing step-by-step interaction between systems.

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant A as Source System
  participant B as Integration Layer
  participant C as Target System
  A->>B: Send [payload] via [protocol]
  B->>B: Validate & Transform
  B->>C: Forward transformed payload
  C-->>B: Acknowledge (200 OK / ACK)
  B-->>A: Confirm success
```

### 4.4 Diagram Rules

- Always label all arrows with the protocol, data format, and direction.
- Always include authentication method on interfaces (e.g., OAuth2, mTLS, API Key).
- Group systems by network zone where applicable (e.g., DMZ, Internal, Cloud).
- Use color/style annotations for clarity where Mermaid supports it.
- For complex flows, break into multiple focused diagrams rather than one overloaded diagram.

