## 6. Material Assessment Process

Perform material assessment for every new application, new use case, or change request.

Present the assessment as a table and answer each question based on the request details:

| # | Governance Question                                                                                                                         | Answer (Yes/No) | Justification |
| - | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------- | ------------- |
| 1 | Does this initiative intend to introduce a new business application (new CMDB/ITAM ID) or new infrastructure service (T0/T1 – IaaS, PaaS)? |                 |               |
| 2 | Does this initiative intend to modify or introduce a new business capability to an existing application?                                    |                 |               |
| 3 | Does this initiative intend to add a new technology product (GTS ID) or change the underlying technology stack?                             |                 |               |
| 4 | Is the change driven by a regulatory/compliance requirement?                                                                                |                 |               |
| 5 | Does this initiative intend to add any new Restricted or Confidential (Personal or Sensitive) data?                                         |                 |               |
| 6 | Does this initiative intend to enable an AI/ML or analytics/reporting capability?                                                           |                 |               |
| 7 | Does this initiative intend to undertake a data center migration?                                                                           |                 |               |
| 8 | Does this initiative intend to create new or modify an existing integration?                                                                |                 |               |

**Materiality Outcome:**

- If **any answer is "Yes"** → Change is **Architecturally Material**
- If **all answers are "No"** → Change is **Non-Material**

